# Expectation record for 03_initializers/008_union_initializers.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 008_union_initializers
area               = 03_initializers
description        = Union initialization and designated union members: a positional initializer selecting the first member, designators naming scalar, aggregate and array members completely and partially, one deliberate legal reinterpretation of an object representation through a second member, a union nested inside a struct between two scalars, and an array of unions mixing designated and positional elements -- nine forms at static duration with three repeated at automatic duration
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined and no unspecified behaviour, which is the precondition that
makes both differential oracles sound: undefined behaviour would license either compiler to do
anything at all, so a divergence over it would prove nothing about either one.
The one construct that has to be justified rather than merely inspected is g_pun, where a union
member other than the one last stored is read. That is LEGAL, not undefined: C11 6.5.2.3 and its
footnote 95 sanction reading a different union member in order to reinterpret an object
representation. Three further facts make the reinterpretation complete and target-invariant here.
sizeof(int) is 4 and b is exactly unsigned char[4], so the four bytes read are precisely the four
bytes of the int and no padding byte is among them -- which matters, because the contents of padding
are unspecified. unsigned char has no trap representations, so each of the four bytes has a
well-defined value. And all four supported targets are little-endian, independently MEASURED, so
0x01020304 reads back as 4, 3, 2, 1 on every backend. The value is read immediately, with nothing
modified in between. Every other union in the program is read through exactly the member its
initializer stored, so no other padding byte is observed and no other object representation is
relied upon.
No uninitialized storage is read anywhere, which is what makes the zero lines assertions rather than
accidents. A positional initializer selects the FIRST member of a union, which C11 6.7.9p17 fixes,
and every designator names a member that exists. Every member or element an initializer does not
name is implicitly zero by C11 6.7.9p19 and p21 -- for automatic duration exactly as for static,
because an object with any initializer is fully initialized -- so g_desig_b_pt.b[1..3],
g_arr_desig.a[0..1] and l_arr_desig.a[0] and a[2] all have determinate values of zero.
No arithmetic is performed beyond the loop counters' increments, bounded by the literals 4 and 3, so
there is no signed overflow. There is no shift of any kind, no division and no remainder. Nothing is
modified after its initialization, so no object is modified twice between two sequence points.
Every subscript is strictly in bounds: i < 4 indexes b[4] and i < 3 indexes a[3], so no
one-past-the-end pointer is even formed, let alone dereferenced. No pointer is cast anywhere -- the
reinterpretation in g_pun goes through a union member access, which is the sanctioned mechanism, and
not through a cast, which would be an aliasing violation. Beyond that access every value is read
through an lvalue of its own declared type: int through int, unsigned through unsigned, and unsigned
char through unsigned char. No address is taken and none is printed, and nothing depends on the
relative addresses of unrelated objects.
Every initializer value is representable in the type it initializes without an implicit conversion
changing it: the signed values are small or -7, the unsigned values are 4000000000u and 52u, both
within the range of a 32-bit unsigned int, and 0x01020304 is within int on every supported target.
Each printf call passes at most one loop counter and one already-narrowed value, neither with a side
effect, so the unspecified order in which a function call's arguments are evaluated cannot be
observed. %d takes int -- including every (int)-cast unsigned char and every (int)sizeof -- and %u
takes unsigned int, matching after the default argument promotions, so no variadic argument is read
at the wrong width.
main returns 0, inside the 0-125 range the suite requires so that no exit status is truncated by the
operating system. Output is fully deterministic: fixed iteration order, no address, no timestamp, no
randomness and no locale-dependent formatting, and nothing outside this file is read, so every cell
is reproducible from this source and this record alone.
No header is included anywhere and no preprocessor directive appears at all; printf is declared by
hand as `int printf(const char *, ...);`. bcc bundles the nine required freestanding headers plus a
bonus stdatomic.h and ships no standard I/O header (docs/project-guide.md line 212), so naming one
would fail on the bcc side of oracle (a) while succeeding on the reference side -- a spurious
divergence caused by the test rather than by a compiler. This area is granted no header exception;
the corpus has exactly two, area 07's stdarg.h and the dedicated bundled-header probe in area 12.
This record declares no warning-gate deviation, and area 03 sanctions none. The program is clean
under the full default gate -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow
-Werror at -O0, -O1 and -O2 with all four reference drivers, and it builds and runs clean under the
sanitizer gate -fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all. Both gates are
reference-compiler-only and are never applied to bcc, so requirement 3's shared-flag discipline is
untouched.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
This record narrows nothing: all four targets, all three optimization levels and all three
oracles are enabled, no expected-divergence marker is carried, and no `ub_audit_flags` key appears
because the program passes the suite's full default warning gate unmodified.
ENDIANNESS IS OBSERVED HERE, DELIBERATELY AND EXACTLY ONCE. g_pun reinterprets a four-byte int
through an unsigned char[4], so the printed byte order depends on the target's byte order. All
four supported targets are little-endian -- recorded in the target table
(docs/technical-specifications.md lines 457-462) and independently MEASURED on each of them -- so
0x01020304 reads back as 4, 3, 2, 1 on every backend. This is the only place in this feature area
that observes an object representation, which makes it a direct cross-backend check on union member
layout rather than an accident. A big-endian target would print the reverse row and would require a
narrowed target list rather than a defect charge; none of the four supported targets is big-endian.
WIDTHS ARE NORMALIZED. Only int, unsigned and unsigned char appear; they are printed with %d and
%u alone, and every unsigned char is cast to int first. No wider integer type, no type whose width
varies by target and no floating type is used anywhere, and no address or pointer value is printed,
so nothing here depends on the MEASURED pointer-width difference on i686 -- four bytes there
against eight on x86-64, AArch64 and RISC-V 64. The source comment deliberately avoids NAMING those
excluded types so that a portability audit grep over this program reports a hit only for a genuine
use; that convention is recorded here rather than repeated there.
PLAIN-CHAR SIGNEDNESS. b is declared unsigned char explicitly rather than plain char, so the
MEASURED split -- signed on x86-64 and i686, unsigned on AArch64 and RISC-V 64 -- cannot reach any
printed byte.
SIZES. The three printed sizes follow only from sizeof(int) == 4 with 4-byte alignment and
sizeof(unsigned char) == 1: sizeof(union simple) is 4, sizeof(union mixed) is max(4, 8, 4) == 8
because struct pair is two ints, and sizeof(union witharr) is max(4, 12) == 12. All of that holds on
all four targets, and each of the three sizes was MEASURED on each of them. The shapes were chosen
so that no padding depends on the alignment of a type whose alignment is 4 on i686 and 8 elsewhere.
EXECUTION CHARACTER SET. No character literal value is printed; the unsigned char bytes printed are
the object representation of an integer, not characters.
THE STATIC/AUTOMATIC PAIRING IS THIS PROGRAM'S DISCRIMINATING VARIANT, and it was verified at
INSTRUCTION level rather than assumed. At -O0 all eleven static objects receive real data images:
g_pun as one four-byte word holding 16909060, g_desig_b as four one-byte values 1, 2, 3 and 4,
g_desig_b_pt as one byte 9 followed by three zero bytes, g_arr_desig as eight zero bytes followed by
the word 33, and g_holder as the three words 41, 42 and 43 in that order; and the three automatic
twins are initialized by stores into the frame. At -O2 not one static object survives -- every value
is folded into an immediate operand of the call that prints it. So -O0 exercises the
initializer-emission path and -O2 the constant-folding path over the same declarations, and both must
produce the recorded bytes. A volatile operand would add nothing here, because the subject is what an
initializer produces rather than what an operator computes -- which is why this program carries no
volatile variant and needs none.
WHERE THE SHAPES DO EXTRA WORK. g_holder is bracketed by tag and trailer so that a designator- or
layout-resolution error shifts one of them rather than only the union member, and each element of
g_uarr is read through the member its own initializer stored -- i, then u, then i again for the
positional element -- so a wrong member selection surfaces as a wrong value rather than as an
unobserved reinterpretation.
MEASURED EVIDENCE. The program was compiled with the reference driver for all four targets at -O0,
-O1 and -O2 -- twelve configurations -- and every one produced these 38 lines byte-identically with
exit status 0, which is why oracle (b) compares this program's targets against each other without
any narrowing and why oracle (c) can hold these bytes as the golden record. Every member and element
is printed on its own line, including the elements an initializer leaves implicitly zero, so a single
divergent line localizes the defect to one initializer form rather than to "one of them".
What would legitimately break these bytes is a big-endian target, which would reverse the four
g_pun.b lines without being defective, or a target where sizeof(int) were not 4, which would change
both the reinterpretation and the three printed sizes. Either would be an implementation-defined
divergence rather than a compiler defect, and must then be recorded as an expected divergence with
this record's target list narrowed and the reason stated in this field -- never left to surface as a
finding against a backend that did nothing wrong, and never resolved by deleting the
reinterpretation or dropping the union coverage this program exists to provide.
END
